      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do you mean by this?\n\nRealistically we have good enough use of the EC based timestamp recording (\"last_interrupt_timestamp \u003d __hw_clock_source_read();\" line). The EC based timestamp recording also handles the drift between the EC and the IMU.\n\nIf HW timestamp refers to a timestamp that the IMU counts internally, I would prefer not to use that (unless you have a good argument to support it).",
      "revId": "727821a4313f41e1036b85342923658dd897e838",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
